COPY public.winam_wisdom_puzzles (id, region, display_text, blank, options, correct_index, original_proverb, difficulty, explanation, created_at) FROM stdin;
yd_yor_066	Yoruba · Nigeria	Ẹni tó bá fọwọ́ kan imú ẹlòmíràn tì í ṣe nítorí pé tirẹ̀ ò jọ rẹ̀ — He who touches another's nose does so because his own does not ____	please him	["please him", "bleed", "smell", "fit"]	0	Ẹni tó bá fọwọ́ kan imú ẹlòmíràn	veteran	Those who meddle in others' affairs or constantly criticise others are usually deflecting from their own inadequacies. Attention directed outward is often avoidance directed inward.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_yor_067	Yoruba · Nigeria	Bí igi bá wó, ẹyẹ tó gbé orí rẹ̀ á máa wá ibì tuntun — When a tree falls the bird that perched on it must find a new ____	branch	["branch", "tree", "home", "ground"]	0	Bí igi bá wó	veteran	Change in circumstances forces adaptation. Those who depend on structures — institutions, patrons, systems — must be ready to find new foundations when those structures fall. Loyalty to a fallen tree is fatal.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_yor_068	Yoruba · Nigeria	Àárọ̀ ni í ṣe ọ̀sán, ọ̀sán ni í ṣe alẹ́ — Morning becomes afternoon, afternoon becomes ____	evening	["evening", "night", "morning", "dusk"]	0	Àárọ̀ ni í ṣe ọ̀sán	veteran	Every stage of life is temporary and transitional. What seems fixed — power, youth, wealth, suffering — is merely a phase passing into the next. This is the Yoruba philosophy of impermanence.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_yor_069	Yoruba · Nigeria	Ẹni tó bá jẹ oúnjẹ ẹlòmíràn ní ìkọ̀kọ̀ yóò sá fún ọmọ rẹ̀ nígbà tí wọn bá ń jẹun — He who eats another's food in secret will flee from his own children at ____	mealtime	["mealtime", "midnight", "harvest", "daybreak"]	0	Ẹni tó bá jẹ oúnjẹ ẹlòmíràn	veteran	Ill-gotten nourishment creates shame that poisons future generations. What you take dishonestly does not build — it corrupts. The consequences of hidden wrong surface in the most intimate moments.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_yor_070	Yoruba · Nigeria	Inú tí kò dára ò ní jẹ kí a jẹun papọ̀ — A bad stomach will not let us eat ____	together	["together", "peacefully", "well", "early"]	0	Inú tí kò dára	veteran	A person of corrupt inner character cannot sustain genuine community. Shared meals — the deepest symbol of trust and unity — are impossible when one party harbours destructive intentions.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_ibo_063	Igbo · Nigeria	Ọ bụ n'oge mmiri na-agba ọsọ ka ọ na-achịkọta ihe nile dị n'ụzọ ya — It is when water is running that it gathers everything in its ____	path	["path", "wake", "stream", "banks"]	0	Ọ bụ n'oge mmiri na-agba ọsọ	veteran	Power and momentum in motion attract resources, followers and opportunities that stillness never could. The right time to build alliances and gather strength is during a period of forward movement — not stagnation.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_ibo_064	Igbo · Nigeria	Onye wetara ji wetara ndụ mana onye richara ya n'ụlọ ya hụghị ọ dị mma — He who brings yam brings life but he who eats it alone in his house has not seen what is ____	good	["good", "enough", "shared", "his"]	0	Onye wetara ji wetara ndụ	veteran	Provision without sharing is incomplete. Life — symbolised by the yam — reaches its fullest expression only in community. Hoarding the very substance of life is a form of spiritual poverty.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_ibo_065	Igbo · Nigeria	Ihe onye hụrụ n'anya ya abụghị ihe onye ọzọ hụrụ n'anya ya — What one person sees with their eyes is not what another sees with ____	theirs	["theirs", "both eyes", "one eye", "the heart"]	0	Ihe onye hụrụ n'anya ya	veteran	Perception is fundamentally subjective and shaped by experience, position and history. Two people witnessing the same event will construct entirely different truths. Wisdom begins by acknowledging this irreducible difference.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_ibo_066	Igbo · Nigeria	Agụ na-atọ ụtọ na-egbu mgbe nile — The leopard that is too comfortable gets ____	killed	["killed", "lazy", "slow", "tame"]	0	Agụ na-atọ ụtọ na-egbu	veteran	Comfort is the predator's most dangerous enemy. Any creature — or person — whose environment becomes too easy, too safe, too predictable, loses the sharpness that survival requires. Ease breeds vulnerability.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_ibo_067	Igbo · Nigeria	Onye na-eme ihe ọ chefuo ihe o ji malite ya ga-adị n'ụzọ — He who acts but forgets what he started with will find it waiting on the ____	road	["road", "way back", "ground", "other side"]	0	Onye na-eme ihe ọ chefuo	veteran	Integrity of purpose — remaining connected to your original intention throughout a journey — is what determines whether arrival means success or failure. Forgetting why you started means arriving somewhere you never intended to go.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_hau_061	Hausa · Nigeria	Wanda ya sani inda zai je ba ya tsoron duhu — He who knows where he is going does not fear the ____	darkness	["darkness", "distance", "road", "unknown"]	0	Wanda ya sani inda zai je ba ya tsoron duhu	veteran	Purpose is the antidote to fear. Uncertainty about destination — not the difficulty of the journey — is what generates anxiety. A person with a clear sense of direction moves through darkness without hesitation.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_hau_062	Hausa · Nigeria	Gaskiya tafi ƙarfe — Truth is stronger than ____	iron	["iron", "lies", "kings", "armies"]	0	Gaskiya tafi ƙarfe	veteran	The Hausa philosophical tradition places truth — gaskiya — above all material and political power. Iron can be bent, armies defeated, kings deposed. Truth, once established, cannot be unmade.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_hau_063	Hausa · Nigeria	Mai girma ba ya yin ihu — The truly great person does not ____	shout	["shout", "beg", "bow", "run"]	0	Mai girma ba ya yin ihu	veteran	Authentic greatness requires no announcement. The person who must declare their own importance has already revealed its absence. Real authority communicates through presence and conduct — not volume.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_hau_064	Hausa · Nigeria	Dodo ya fi tsoro fiye da yadda yake da shi — The monster is more frightening in the ____ than in reality	imagination	["imagination", "dark", "story", "forest"]	0	Dodo ya fi tsoro	veteran	Fear of the imagined is almost always worse than the reality encountered. The mind constructs monsters that the world rarely delivers. Courage is often simply the act of looking directly at what you have been imagining.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_hau_065	Hausa · Nigeria	Lokacin da zakara ya yi kukan safe ba shi ne ya sa alfijir ba — When the rooster crows at dawn it is not the rooster that ____	makes the dawn	["makes the dawn", "wakes the sun", "starts the day", "calls the birds"]	0	Lokacin da zakara ya yi kukan safe	veteran	Heralding an event is not the same as causing it. Those who announce or celebrate change rarely created it. The rooster claims the dawn it merely observed. True causation is usually quieter and less visible than its announcers.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_aka_061	Akan · Ghana	Obi nnim ade a ɔde bebrebe so — No one knows the thing that is ____	too heavy to carry	["too heavy to carry", "worth stealing", "truly his own", "beyond counting"]	0	Obi nnim ade a ɔde bebrebe so	veteran	The limits of any burden are unknown until you have carried it. What appears impossibly heavy from a distance is often survivable up close — and what seems manageable can destroy you over time. You never know your true capacity until tested.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_aka_062	Akan · Ghana	Ɔpanyin na ɔnim sɛ anomaa bi retwa kwan — It is the elder who knows that a certain bird is crossing the ____	path	["path", "river", "sky", "boundary"]	0	Ɔpanyin na ɔnim sɛ anomaa bi retwa kwan	veteran	Experience grants perception that youth cannot access. The elder reads signs — subtle movements, seasonal patterns, behavioral cues — that are invisible to those without the accumulation of years. This is why elders must be consulted.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_aka_063	Akan · Ghana	Wo se wo behu adee a na wo ani da so — If you say you will see something your ____  must be open	eyes	["eyes", "heart", "mind", "ears"]	0	Wo se wo behu adee a na wo ani da so	veteran	Intent without attentiveness is empty. You cannot receive what you claim to be seeking if you are not genuinely alert and present to its arrival. Openness is not passive — it is an active, disciplined state of receptivity.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_aka_064	Akan · Ghana	Ɛfiri se ɔhene te ase a na n'amammui na ɛsɛe — When a chief is beneath his subjects it is his ____  that is destroyed	reputation	["reputation", "throne", "family", "village"]	0	Ɛfiri se ɔhene te ase a	veteran	A leader who falls below the standard of those they lead loses not merely respect but the entire framework of their authority. Leadership is a moral position before it is a political one — the moment the character fails the institution collapses.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_aka_065	Akan · Ghana	Nyansa na ɛma wo hu sɛ w'ani bere — It is wisdom that makes you see that your ____  is ripe	time	["time", "fruit", "harvest", "chance"]	0	Nyansa na ɛma wo hu sɛ w'ani bere	veteran	Wisdom is not just knowledge — it is timing. Knowing what to do is only half the skill. Knowing when the moment has arrived, when conditions are ripe for action, is the deeper and rarer form of intelligence.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_swa_066	Swahili · East Africa	Asiyejua maana ya leo hatajua la ____	kesho	["kesho", "jana", "sasa", "wakati"]	0	Asiyejua maana ya leo hatajua la kesho	veteran	He who does not know the meaning of today will not know tomorrow. Present awareness is the precondition for future wisdom. Those who sleepwalk through their current circumstances arrive at the future without the understanding needed to navigate it.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_swa_067	Swahili · East Africa	Bahari ya elimu haifiki ____	pwani	["pwani", "chini", "juu", "kati"]	0	Bahari ya elimu haifiki pwani	veteran	The ocean of knowledge has no shore. Learning is truly infinite — there is no point at which a person can legitimately say they have arrived at the edge of what can be known. This makes humility before knowledge a permanent condition, not a temporary one.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_swa_068	Swahili · East Africa	Chovya chovya humaliza ____	buyu la asali	["buyu la asali", "mto", "nguvu", "muda"]	0	Chovya chovya humaliza buyu la asali	veteran	Drop by drop empties the honey gourd. Patient, persistent, incremental extraction — whether of resources, knowledge or opportunity — accomplishes what no single dramatic effort could. This is the deep logic behind consistent small actions over time.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_swa_069	Swahili · East Africa	Damu nzito kuliko ____	maji	["maji", "ardhi", "dhahabu", "nguvu"]	0	Damu nzito kuliko maji	veteran	Blood is thicker than water. The bonds of kinship carry a weight that no friendship, alliance or contract can fully replicate. When everything else dissolves, family — with all its complexity — remains the most durable human attachment.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_swa_070	Swahili · East Africa	Mvua ya usiku hairudishi ____ wa mchana	jua	["jua", "shamba", "jasho", "wakati"]	0	Mvua ya usiku hairudishi jua wa mchana	veteran	The night rain cannot restore the sun of day. Some losses are irreversible — no subsequent abundance can replace what was present at the right time and then lost. Timing is not merely important; for some things it is everything.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_zul_061	Zulu · South Africa	Inyoka ingena endlini ngomnyango — A snake enters a house through the ____	door	["door", "window", "crack", "darkness"]	0	Inyoka ingena endlini ngomnyango	veteran	Danger enters through openings you yourself have created or left unguarded. The breach that allows destruction is almost never an external assault — it is an internal failure of vigilance. What you leave open invites what you fear.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_zul_062	Zulu · South Africa	Izimu zidla abantu abangazi — Monsters eat people who do not ____	know	["know", "run", "fight", "pray"]	0	Izimu zidla abantu abangazi	veteran	Ignorance is not innocence — it is vulnerability. The forces that exploit people do not target the strong or the prepared; they consume those who lack the knowledge to recognise and resist them. Knowing is itself a form of protection.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_zul_063	Zulu · South Africa	Umuntu ka pheli efa — A person never truly finishes ____	dying	["dying", "living", "learning", "giving"]	0	Umuntu ka pheli efa	veteran	Death is not a single moment but a process — and conversely, so is life. The Zulu understanding of personhood sees continuity between the living and the ancestors. Those who have died continue to exist in a form that influences the living.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_zul_064	Zulu · South Africa	Izulu liyabika — The sky ____	announces	["announces", "lies", "forgets", "changes"]	0	Izulu liyabika	veteran	Nature communicates its intentions clearly to those who know how to read it. The skilled person — farmer, hunter, elder — reads the sky before acting. All of reality broadcasts its next move; wisdom is learning to receive the signal.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_zul_065	Zulu · South Africa	Amathe ayabuyela emthonjeni — Saliva returns to its ____	source	["source", "mouth", "ground", "owner"]	0	Amathe ayabuyela emthonjeni	veteran	What originates in you returns to you — words, actions, energy, consequences. The Zulu conception of moral reciprocity holds that no act is truly complete until it has cycled back to its origin. Everything you release into the world finds its way home.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_eth_059	Amharic · Ethiopia	Lijun yemiyawud hager yemiyawud new — The country that loves its children is the country that ____	raises them well	["raises them well", "protects them", "feeds them", "teaches them"]	0	Lijun yemiyawud hager yemiyawud new	veteran	Love without investment is sentiment, not love. A nation — or family, or community — demonstrates genuine love for its children not through affection alone but through the quality of what it builds for and in them. Love is measured by what it produces.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_eth_060	Amharic · Ethiopia	Ye'algebra lij key lij nat — The algebra child is a ____  child	red	["red", "smart", "hidden", "borrowed"]	0	Ye'algebra lij key lij nat	veteran	In Ethiopian tradition this speaks to mixed or uncertain origin — the child whose background is complex or disputed. More broadly it addresses the anxiety around legitimacy, belonging and identity that arises when origins are unclear or contested.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_ibo_022	Igbo · Nigeria	When a fowl drinks water it shows gratitude to ____	God	["God", "the sky", "the earth", "the rain"]	0	Mgbe ọkụkọ na-ażụ mmiri, o nyefee ọchịchọ ọchịchọ n'elu igwe	beginner	Gratitude should flow upward toward the source of all provision. Acknowledging where our sustenance comes from is both honest and spiritually essential.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_eth_061	Amharic · Ethiopia	Inde lijoch new yeminnoru — It is like children that they ____	live	["live", "play", "argue", "forget"]	0	Inde lijoch new yeminnoru	veteran	Those who live with innocence, presence and uncalculated joy inhabit existence most fully. The adult who has retained the child's quality of pure engagement with the present moment has achieved something rare and precious.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_eth_062	Amharic · Ethiopia	Neger bizu new yemibale — There is much that is called ____	a thing	["a thing", "nothing", "everything", "truth"]	0	Neger bizu new yemibale	veteran	Language and naming inflate the apparent substance of the world. Many things called significant are not. The wise person develops the ability to distinguish between what is truly substantial and what merely carries the name of substance.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_wol_058	Wolof · Senegal	Lu xiif tax lool dafa tax buur di dëkk — What extreme hunger causes is that even a ____ will beg	king	["king", "chief", "elder", "warrior"]	0	Lu xiif tax lool dafa tax buur di dëkk	veteran	Extreme deprivation strips away all social performance and pretence. Hunger — the most primal need — reduces every human being to their bare vulnerability regardless of rank. This is simultaneously a warning about poverty and a meditation on the fragility of status.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_wol_059	Wolof · Senegal	Ku am sa bopp am sa ____	xel	["xel", "doom", "dëkk", "yëkënam"]	0	Ku am sa bopp am sa xel	veteran	He who has his own head has his own mind. True autonomy begins with the capacity for independent thought. A person who cannot form their own judgments is not truly their own person regardless of their external freedom.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_wol_060	Wolof · Senegal	Doom ji mën a jaay nit ki — A child can ____  a person	sell	["sell", "surpass", "shame", "save"]	0	Doom ji mën a jaay nit ki	veteran	A child's actions can reduce an adult to a kind of social destruction — betraying family secrets, acting shamefully, or revealing what parents wished hidden. The power of children over the reputation of their elders is absolute and often underestimated.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_081	Pan-African	The one who sets the trap does not always catch what they ____	intended	["intended", "feared", "deserved", "planted"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Consequences are rarely as precise as intentions. What you engineer to harm another may catch you instead; what you design to capture one thing may release another. The trap-setter's assumption of control is always partial.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_082	Pan-African	He who does not know can know — but he who does not want to know cannot be ____	taught	["taught", "reached", "saved", "trusted"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Ignorance is curable. Wilful ignorance — the choice not to know, not to grow, not to be corrected — is the only truly incurable intellectual condition. The barrier to learning is never capacity; it is always will.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_083	Pan-African	The river that forgets its source will dry ____	up	["up", "out", "away", "completely"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Identity and sustenance require an unbroken connection to origin. Individuals, communities and nations that sever their relationship with where they came from lose the underground current that keeps them flowing. Rootlessness is a slow desiccation.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_084	Pan-African	What you help to build you have no right to ____	destroy	["destroy", "own", "leave", "sell"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Participation in creation carries moral obligation toward what was created. You cannot invest your hands in building something and then claim the right to tear it down. This applies to families, communities, institutions — anything built in collaboration.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_085	Pan-African	The child who is carried does not know how long the ____  is	road	["road", "journey", "path", "way"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Those who are protected from difficulty by others' labour remain ignorant of the true cost of what sustains them. Ease conceals the distance. Only the one who walks knows what the road demands — and what it took to travel it.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_086	Pan-African	Rain does not choose to fall on the just and avoid the ____	unjust	["unjust", "poor", "wicked", "weak"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Nature makes no moral distinctions. Rain, sun, drought and flood arrive without regard for desert or worthiness. The universe is not arranged to reward the good and punish the bad through natural events. Human justice must be built — it is not given.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_001	Pan-African	It takes a ____ to raise a child	village	["village", "mother", "father", "elder"]	0	Inachukua kijiji kulea mtoto	beginner	No single person can provide everything a child needs to become whole. The full development of a human being requires the collective investment of an entire community across time.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_002	Pan-African	When the music changes so does the ____	dance	["dance", "singer", "drum", "crowd"]	0	Muziki ukibadilika, ngoma nayo inabadilika	beginner	When circumstances change our response must change with them. Rigidly applying the same approach regardless of shifting conditions leads to irrelevance and failure.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_003	Pan-African	The ____ does not know the shape of its own back	monkey	["monkey", "elephant", "lion", "buffalo"]	0	Tumbili haijui umbo la mgongo wake	intermediate	We are often the last to see what is most obvious about ourselves. Our blind spots are precisely the things most visible to everyone around us.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_004	Pan-African	Rain does not fall on one man's ____	farm	["farm", "roof", "head", "path"]	0	Mvua hainyeshi shamba la mtu mmoja tu	beginner	Hardship and blessing do not target individuals — they fall on everyone. Shared conditions create shared humanity and remind us that no one is exempt from the fundamental experiences of life.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_005	Pan-African	However long the night the ____ will rise	dawn	["dawn", "moon", "sun", "star"]	0	Hata usiku mrefu kiasi gani mapambazuko yatakuja	beginner	Difficulty is not permanent. No matter how long or dark a period of suffering may be it will eventually give way to something new. Endurance is what carries us to that transition.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_006	Pan-African	If you want to go fast go alone if you want to go ____ go together	far	["far", "slow", "safely", "first"]	0	Ukitaka kwenda haraka nenda peke yako ukitaka kwenda mbali nenda pamoja	beginner	Speed and distance require fundamentally different strategies. Moving fast is a solo achievement but reaching far requires collective effort and sustained cooperation.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_007	Pan-African	The ____ that is not watered will not grow	seed	["seed", "child", "dream", "fire"]	0	Mbegu isiyomwagiliwa haitamea	beginner	Growth requires consistent investment over time. Dreams ambitions and relationships wither without the regular nourishment of attention effort and care.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_008	Pan-African	A tree is straightened while it is still ____	young	["young", "green", "small", "growing"]	0	Mti hunyooshwa ukiwa bado mchanga	beginner	Character is most effectively shaped early in life before patterns become rigid. The time to establish good values and habits is during formative years not after they have calcified.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_088	Pan-African	You cannot climb to the top of a tree and be afraid of ____	heights	["heights", "falling", "the view", "the top"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Commitment to a path requires accepting its full implications. You cannot pursue ambition and then recoil from what ambition requires. To choose the climb is to choose the exposure — they are inseparable. Half-commitment is a contradiction.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_089	Pan-African	The wise do not sit by the road to watch how ____  others walk	awkwardly	["awkwardly", "quickly", "slowly", "proudly"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Wisdom is too demanding of attention to be wasted on the observation and criticism of others' flaws. The genuinely wise are too occupied with their own path, growth and duties to position themselves as judges of other people's gait.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_pan_090	Pan-African	Speak less than you know — give less than you ____	have	["have", "owe", "earn", "need"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Restraint in speech and generosity in reserve are the marks of sustainable power. Those who speak everything they know and give everything they have leave themselves exposed and depleted. Hold more than you show — always.	2026-05-24 00:29:03.071775+00
yd_hau_013	Hausa · Nigeria	The ____ knows its own pond	frog	["frog", "fish", "hippo", "crane"]	0	Kwado ya san tafkinsa	beginner	Every creature has an intimate knowledge of its own natural environment and conditions. We are each most expert in the territory we actually inhabit and experience directly.	2026-04-19 00:38:43.408689+00
yd_zul_001	Zulu · South Africa	A person is a person through other ____	people	["people", "deeds", "words", "struggles"]	0	Umuntu ngumuntu ngabantu	beginner	Our humanity is not a solitary achievement — it is constituted through our relationships and interactions with others. We become fully human only through the community that shapes receives and reflects us.	2026-04-19 01:01:44.219251+00
yd_swa_012	Swahili · East Africa	Unity is ____ and division is weakness	strength	["strength", "peace", "wealth", "beauty"]	0	Umoja ni nguvu na utengano ni udhaifu	beginner	When people stand together they become capable of withstanding forces that would easily overcome any individual among them. Division is the primary source of vulnerability.	2026-04-19 00:32:43.535104+00
yd_pan_009	Pan-African	Knowledge is like a ____ the more you share it the more you have	fire	["fire", "river", "garden", "wind"]	0	Maarifa ni kama moto unaoongezeka unaposhirikiwa	intermediate	Sharing knowledge does not diminish the sharer — it multiplies the impact. Unlike physical resources wisdom grows rather than shrinks when it is distributed freely.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_010	Pan-African	A child who is not taught will sell the house his ____ built	father	["father", "mother", "grandfather", "village"]	0	Mtoto asiyefunzwa atauzа nyumba aliyoijenga baba yake	beginner	A child who receives education rather than just material inheritance is truly equipped for life. Knowledge cannot be stolen divided or depleted the way possessions can.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_011	Pan-African	Until the lion learns to ____ every story will glorify the hunter	write	["write", "speak", "hunt", "roar"]	0	Mpaka simba ajifunze kuandika kila hadithi itamtukuza mwindaji	intermediate	Those who control how history and current events are told control how people understand reality. Narrative power is one of the most consequential and often overlooked forms of influence.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_swa_034	Swahili · East Africa	A wound inflicted by a ____ heals but one inflicted by the tongue does not	sword	["sword", "stone", "spear", "stick"]	0	Jeraha la upanga huponya lakini la ulimi haliponyi	intermediate	Words penetrate and damage in ways that physical injuries do not. The body heals from most wounds but the harm done by harsh words can be permanent and deep.	2026-04-19 00:32:43.535104+00
yd_pan_012	Pan-African	The ____ that falls alone does not make a forest	tree	["tree", "leaf", "rain", "seed"]	0	Mti unaoanguka peke yake haufanyi msitu	intermediate	A single isolated event or person cannot create the conditions for lasting change. Meaningful transformation requires accumulation repetition and the coming together of many forces.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_013	Pan-African	Wisdom is not in the ____ it is in the mind	eyes	["eyes", "hands", "feet", "tongue"]	0	Hekima haiko machoni bali inapatikana akilini	intermediate	True wisdom is not visible on the surface — it is an internal quality developed through experience and reflection. Appearance and intelligence are completely independent of each other.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_014	Pan-African	An army of ____ can defeat an elephant	ants	["ants", "spears", "arrows", "drums"]	0	Jeshi la mchwa linaweza kumshinda tembo	beginner	Collective and persistent effort can overcome even the most overwhelming individual power. Numbers coordination and determination can defeat advantages of size and strength.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_015	Pan-African	The ____ that does not speak does not eat	child	["child", "elder", "hunter", "farmer"]	0	Mtoto asiyelia halii	beginner	Advocating for your needs is essential to having them met. Those who remain silent about what they require cannot expect others to intuit and provide it.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_016	Pan-African	A man who uses force is afraid of ____	reasoning	["reasoning", "failure", "strangers", "darkness"]	0	Mtu anayetumia nguvu anaogopa hoja	intermediate	Aggression and domination are symptoms of an inability to engage through reason and persuasion. Those who resort to force have typically exhausted their capacity for legitimate argument.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_017	Pan-African	Not everyone who chased the zebra caught it but whoever caught it chased ____	it	["it", "hard", "long", "well"]	0	Si kila aliyemfuatia punda milia alimkamata lakini aliyemkamata alimfuatia	advanced	Results require committed sustained pursuit. Everyone who achieves something difficult went through the same process of relentless effort — achievement and effort are inseparable.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_018	Pan-African	The ____ shared among friends does not fill the stomach	meal	["meal", "secret", "burden", "story"]	0	Chakula kilichoshirikiwa miongoni mwa marafiki hakijazi tumbo	intermediate	What is divided among many cannot fully satisfy any individual among them. There are things that require wholeness to deliver their full value and cannot be meaningfully shared.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_019	Pan-African	A person with a ____ does not realise its weight	hump	["hump", "burden", "gift", "wound"]	0	Mtu mwenye nundu haihisi uzito wake	advanced	We often cannot perceive our own most defining characteristics because we are too close to them. The things most obvious about us are frequently invisible to us alone.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_020	Pan-African	The ____ does not hate the rain	earth	["earth", "farmer", "river", "cloud"]	0	Ardhi haichuki mvua	beginner	The natural world accepts what comes to it without resistance or complaint. There is wisdom in receiving what arrives rather than fighting against what cannot be changed.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_021	Pan-African	If the cockroach wants to rule over the ____ it must first get rid of the chicken	chicken	["chicken", "house", "farm", "field"]	0	Kama mende anataka kutawala kuku lazima aondoe kuku kwanza	advanced	Eliminating a threat requires addressing the conditions that make that threat possible. You cannot solve a problem while the thing enabling it remains untouched.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_042	Pan-African	The ____ of a lie runs short	leg	["leg", "life", "shadow", "reward"]	0	Mguu wa uongo ni mfupi	beginner	Deception is inherently unstable and self-limiting. A lie requires more lies to sustain it and eventually collapses under the weight of its own contradictions.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_022	Pan-African	The ____ does not drink the water it carries	cloud	["cloud", "river", "pot", "hand"]	0	Wingu halikunywi maji linaloyabeba	intermediate	Those entrusted with carrying things for others do not personally benefit from what they carry. Service is its own category distinct from ownership and enjoyment.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_023	Pan-African	Speak ____ so your words can be heard across mountains	softly	["softly", "boldly", "slowly", "clearly"]	0	Sema polepole ili maneno yako yasikiwe ng'ambo ya milima	intermediate	The manner of delivery matters as much as the content of what is delivered. Even the most important message can be lost or rejected if it is communicated with insufficient care.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_024	Pan-African	The ____ of one person is the wealth of many	knowledge	["knowledge", "loss", "struggle", "hunger"]	0	Maarifa ya mtu mmoja ni utajiri wa wengi	beginner	What one person knows benefits everyone who can access that knowledge. Individual learning has communal value that extends far beyond the person who did the learning.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_025	Pan-African	A patient person will always eat ____ meat	ripe	["ripe", "fresh", "sweet", "soft"]	0	Mtu mwenye subira daima atakula nyama iliyoiva	beginner	Patience is what allows things to fully develop and reach their best possible state. Rushing toward results before they are ready produces inferior outcomes compared to waiting for maturity.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_026	Pan-African	A healthy ear can ____ a sick one	tolerate	["tolerate", "hear", "teach", "heal"]	0	Sikio zuri linaweza kuvumilia lile lililougua	intermediate	The capacity to tolerate discomfort and difference is itself a form of healing and strength. Acceptance of others requires a kind of internal health that must be actively cultivated.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_027	Pan-African	The forest would be silent if no ____ sang except the one that sang best	bird	["bird", "animal", "man", "tree"]	0	Msitu ungekuwa kimya kama ndege hawangepiga sauti isipokuwa yule bora zaidi	advanced	Demanding perfection before allowing participation silences the majority of potential contributors. The world would be impoverished if only the most exceptional voices were permitted to speak.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_028	Pan-African	The ____ that travels far knows many roads	traveller	["traveller", "wind", "river", "bird"]	0	Msafiri anayesafiri mbali anajua njia nyingi	beginner	Exposure to diverse experiences and places accumulates as a form of practical knowledge. Those who move through many different contexts develop a richness of understanding that the stationary cannot acquire.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_029	Pan-African	A man who pays respect to the great paves the way for his own ____	greatness	["greatness", "safety", "wealth", "journey"]	0	Mtu anayeheshimu wakuu hufungua njia ya ukuu wake mwenyewe	intermediate	Honouring those who have achieved greatness creates the cultural conditions for future greatness to emerge. Reverence for excellence signals that excellence is valued and worth pursuing.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_030	Pan-African	When spider ____ unite they can tie up a lion	webs	["webs", "legs", "eyes", "eggs"]	0	Nyuzi za buibui zikiunganishwa zinaweza kumfunga simba	intermediate	Small things combined with intention and coordination can overcome forces that seem insurmountably larger. Scale alone does not determine outcome when organisation and persistence are present.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_031	Pan-African	You do not teach the ____ to swim	fish	["fish", "river", "child", "frog"]	0	Haufundishi samaki kuogelea	beginner	Expertise in any domain carries its own inherent logic that cannot be imposed from outside. You cannot instruct mastery into someone — it must be developed from within through practice.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_032	Pan-African	The ____ does not make fun of the impala for having no horns	buffalo	["buffalo", "giraffe", "zebra", "elephant"]	0	Nyati haimdhihaki mpala kwa kukosa pembe	intermediate	Mocking others for what they lack reveals more about the mocker's insecurity than about the person being mocked. True confidence does not require diminishing others.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_033	Pan-African	He who ____ at others digs two graves	hates	["hates", "laughs", "lies", "shouts"]	0	Anayewachukia wengine huchimba makaburi mawili	intermediate	Hatred is self-destructive — it costs the hater more than it costs the hated. Carrying animosity toward others is a burden that damages primarily the one carrying it.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_034	Pan-African	A ____ does not return to its shell	butterfly	["butterfly", "snail", "crab", "turtle"]	0	Kipepeo hakirudi kwenye ganda lake	beginner	Growth and transformation are irreversible. Once genuine development has occurred there is no returning to a previous and lesser state of being.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_035	Pan-African	The ____ of a good tree is always sweet	fruit	["fruit", "shade", "bark", "root"]	0	Tunda la mti mzuri daima ni tamu	beginner	What emerges from good foundations tends to be good. The quality of outcomes is determined largely by the quality of the conditions and care that produced them.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_036	Pan-African	Only a fool ____ the river he has not yet crossed	tests	["tests", "crosses", "praises", "fears"]	0	Mjinga tu ndiye anayejaribu mto ambao bado hajavuka	intermediate	Caution before commitment prevents many preventable disasters. Assessing the nature of what you are entering before you are fully inside it is simple practical wisdom.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_037	Pan-African	The ____ goes where it is sent not where it wants	messenger	["messenger", "wind", "river", "bird"]	0	Mjumbe huenda alipotumwa si alipotaka	beginner	Those sent to accomplish a task are bound by the parameters of their mission not by their own preferences. Service means subordinating personal desire to the purpose you have been given.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_038	Pan-African	A full ____ does not know what a hungry one feels	stomach	["stomach", "purse", "heart", "hand"]	0	Tumbo lililoshiba halijui hisia za lile lenye njaa	beginner	Those who are comfortable cannot truly understand the perspective of those who are suffering. Privilege creates a perceptual gap that requires deliberate effort to bridge.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_039	Pan-African	Do not set sail using someone else's ____	star	["star", "wind", "boat", "compass"]	0	Usisafiri kwa kutumia nyota ya mtu mwingine	intermediate	The guidance we use to navigate our lives should come from our own deepest values not from borrowed frameworks that do not truly fit our situation and identity.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_040	Pan-African	The ____ does not hate the ground that holds its roots	tree	["tree", "river", "wind", "rain"]	0	Mti hauchuki ardhi inayoshikilia mizizi yake	beginner	What has consistently supported and sustained us deserves our loyalty and gratitude. We should not turn against the very things that have been our foundation.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_041	Pan-African	When two elephants ____ it is the grass that suffers	fight	["fight", "walk", "eat", "play"]	0	Tembo wawili wanapopigana nyasi ndizo zinazoumia	beginner	When powerful forces conflict it is always those with the least power who absorb the most damage. The consequences of conflict among the powerful fall disproportionately on the vulnerable.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_043	Pan-African	He who learns ____ must first learn to walk	to run	["to run", "to fight", "to lead", "to speak"]	0	Anayejifunza kukimbia lazima kwanza ajifunze kutembea	beginner	Foundational skills and capacities must precede more complex ones. There is a natural sequence to development that cannot be safely skipped without creating dangerous gaps.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_044	Pan-African	The ____ you help today may carry you tomorrow	person	["person", "child", "stranger", "elder"]	0	Mtu unayemsaidia leo anaweza kukubeba kesho	beginner	The assistance we provide today creates the social fabric of reciprocity that supports us when we are in need. Generosity is a form of investment in the community that will eventually return to us.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_045	Pan-African	A wound heals but the ____ of it remains	scar	["scar", "pain", "memory", "story"]	0	Jeraha huponya lakini kovu lake linabaki	beginner	The evidence of what we have endured remains even after the enduring is over. Our histories are written on us in ways that do not fully disappear even when the pain fades.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_046	Pan-African	Do not look down on the one who carries your ____	load	["load", "child", "secret", "name"]	0	Usimdhihaki anayebeba mzigo wako	intermediate	Those who benefit from the service of others owe them basic dignity and respect. Contempt toward the people whose work sustains you is both unjust and self-defeating.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_047	Pan-African	The ____ that knows no boundaries runs dry	river	["river", "dream", "heart", "fire"]	0	Mto usiojua mipaka wake hukauka	advanced	Systems and relationships that refuse to acknowledge their own limits eventually exhaust their resources entirely. Sustainable existence requires awareness of and respect for natural boundaries.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_048	Pan-African	A man's ____ is not judged by what he has but by what he gives	wealth	["wealth", "worth", "name", "strength"]	0	Utajiri wa mtu haupimwi na alichonacho bali anachokipa	intermediate	True value is demonstrated through what we contribute not through what we accumulate. The measure of a person's worth is found in their generosity not their possessions.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_049	Pan-African	The ____ does not forget the hand that fed it	dog	["dog", "bird", "child", "horse"]	0	Mbwa hausahau mkono uliousha	beginner	Loyalty and gratitude are deeply encoded in those who have been genuinely cared for. Kindness leaves a permanent impression that outlasts the moment in which it was given.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_pan_050	Pan-African	Wisdom is ____ you can always add to it but never take away	water	["water", "fire", "gold", "light"]	0	Hekima ni kama maji unaweza kuongeza lakini si kupunguza	advanced	Wisdom is not diminished by sharing — it is enriched and deepened through the process of transmission. Unlike finite resources knowledge grows through distribution rather than shrinking.	2026-04-19 00:34:41.221742+00
yd_yor_051	Yoruba · Nigeria	Ọmọ tí a kò kọ ni yóò ta ilé tí a kọ — A child who is not ____ will burn down the house that was built	taught	["taught", "fed", "loved", "sheltered"]	0	Ọmọ tí a kò kọ ni yóò ta ilé tí a kọ	beginner	Children who are not properly educated and guided will ultimately destroy the very foundations their families worked hard to build.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
