yd_ibo_051	Igbo · Nigeria	Onye wetara oji wetara ____ — He who brings kola brings life	life	["life", "peace", "joy", "wisdom"]	0	Onye wetara oji wetara ndụ	beginner	The kola nut is sacred in Igbo culture. This proverb speaks to generosity as a life-giving force — sharing creates community.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_ibo_052	Igbo · Nigeria	Egbe bere ugo bere nke si ibe ya ebena nku kwa ya — Let the eagle perch and let the ____ perch	hawk	["hawk", "dove", "crow", "owl"]	0	Egbe bere ugo bere	beginner	Live and let live. Neither the eagle nor the hawk should deny the other its right to exist. A call for mutual respect among equals.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
