yd_aka_051	Akan · Ghana	Onipa na ohwehwe onipa — It is a ____ who looks for a ____	person	["person", "elder", "chief", "hunter"]	0	Onipa na ohwehwe onipa	beginner	Only human beings can truly understand and seek out other human beings. Our shared humanity is what draws us into community and relationship.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_052	Akan · Ghana	Obi nkyere obi agyinamoa — No one shows another the ____	cat	["cat", "way", "chief", "forest"]	0	Obi nkyere obi agyinamoa	intermediate	A cat finds its own way instinctively. Some knowledge is innate — and imposing guidance where none is needed is disrespectful.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_053	Akan · Ghana	Obra ye osubban — Life is like a ____	river	["river", "market", "farm", "mountain"]	0	Obra ye osubban	intermediate	Like a river, life flows continuously, changes direction, encounters obstacles and finds its way through. Adaptability is the key to living well.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_054	Akan · Ghana	Sika ye mogya — Money is ____	blood	["blood", "water", "power", "fire"]	0	Sika ye mogya	advanced	Money flows through society the way blood flows through a body — it gives life and sustains function when it circulates but is deadly when it stops or is hoarded.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_055	Akan · Ghana	Nyansa bu mmere — Wisdom breaks the ____	stone	["stone", "road", "yam", "day"]	0	Nyansa bu mmere	intermediate	True wisdom overcomes even the hardest obstacles. No physical barrier is proof against a truly wise mind that approaches it correctly.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_056	Akan · Ghana	Tumi nyinaa firi Onyame — All power comes from ____	God	["God", "the chief", "the people", "the ancestors"]	0	Tumi nyinaa firi Onyame	beginner	Ultimate authority and power are divine gifts, not human possessions. This keeps leaders humble and accountable to a higher order.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_057	Akan · Ghana	Ɛfiri se animguase mfata Ɔkanni ba — Disgrace does not befit a child of the ____	Gold Coast	["Gold Coast", "forest", "river", "chief"]	0	Ɛfiri se animguase mfata Ɔkanni ba	advanced	A person of noble heritage must conduct themselves with corresponding dignity. Your origins place expectations on your behaviour.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_058	Akan · Ghana	Wo nsa da mu a — When your hand is in the ____	pot	["pot", "ground", "fire", "crowd"]	0	Wo nsa da mu a	intermediate	When you are involved in something — especially something risky — you cannot act as if you are separate from it. Full commitment requires accepting full responsibility.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_059	Akan · Ghana	Ɔkoto nwo anoma — A crab does not give birth to a ____	bird	["bird", "fish", "spider", "snake"]	0	Ɔkoto nwo anoma	beginner	Like begets like. You cannot expect something fundamentally different to come from what you are — you produce according to your nature.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_aka_060	Akan · Ghana	Esono nni hu a na na ne ba na ehuu — The elephant does not fear but its child ____	does	["does", "runs", "hides", "cries"]	0	Esono nni hu a na na ne ba na ehuu	advanced	Courage in parents does not automatically transfer to children. Each generation must develop its own strength and face its own fears.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_052	Swahili · East Africa	Umoja ni nguvu, utengano ni ____ — Unity is strength, division is ____	weakness	["weakness", "death", "silence", "shame"]	0	Umoja ni nguvu, utengano ni udhaifu	beginner	The most fundamental African political principle: divided people are vulnerable people. Strength comes only through collective unity.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_053	Swahili · East Africa	Mtu ni watu — A person is ____	people	["people", "alone", "spirit", "earth"]	0	Mtu ni watu	beginner	A human being is defined and completed by their community. You are not fully yourself in isolation — personhood is fundamentally relational.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_054	Swahili · East Africa	Asiye na ____ hana kinga — He who has no shame has no ____	shield	["shield", "shame", "name", "home"]	0	Asiye na haya hana kinga	intermediate	Shame is not weakness — it is the internal compass that protects you from disgrace. Without it you have no defence against your own worst impulses.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_055	Swahili · East Africa	Bahari haizuii mto — The ____ does not stop the ____	sea	["sea", "mountain", "wind", "storm"]	0	Bahari haizuii mto	intermediate	The ocean does not block the river — it receives it. Great forces do not always oppose each other; sometimes they merge and accommodate each other.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_056	Swahili · East Africa	Dawa ya moto ni ____ — The cure for fire is ____	fire	["fire", "water", "wind", "earth"]	0	Dawa ya moto ni moto	advanced	Sometimes the only way to fight a fierce problem is with an equally fierce response. Gentle approaches do not always work against powerful forces.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_057	Swahili · East Africa	Elimu haina ____ — Knowledge has no ____	end	["end", "price", "enemy", "colour"]	0	Elimu haina mwisho	beginner	Learning is infinite. No matter how much you know there is always more to discover — humility before knowledge lasts a lifetime.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_058	Swahili · East Africa	Fuata nyuki ule ____ — Follow the bee and eat the ____	honey	["honey", "flower", "fruit", "wax"]	0	Fuata nyuki ule asali	beginner	If you follow someone with knowledge and skill you will share in their rewards. Discipleship and mentorship lead to real benefits.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_059	Swahili · East Africa	Haba na haba hujaza ____ — Little by little fills the ____	jar	["jar", "river", "granary", "basket"]	0	Haba na haba hujaza kibaba	beginner	Consistent small efforts accumulate into great results. Do not despise small daily progress — it is the only path to significant achievement.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_060	Swahili · East Africa	Jogoo la shamba haliwiki ____ — A village rooster does not crow in the ____	city	["city", "rain", "dark", "cold"]	0	Jogoo la shamba haliwiki mjini	intermediate	Skills and authority appropriate in one context may not transfer to another. Know where your competence genuinely applies.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_061	Swahili · East Africa	Mchezo wa kuigiza hauishi — A game of pretending never ____	ends	["ends", "wins", "helps", "pays"]	0	Mchezo wa kuigiza hauishi	advanced	Deception and pretence cannot be sustained indefinitely. Eventually reality asserts itself and the performance collapses.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_062	Swahili · East Africa	Ndoto za mchana hutekelezwa na ____ — Daydreams are implemented by ____	action	["action", "night", "angels", "luck"]	0	Ndoto za mchana hutekelezwa na vitendo	intermediate	Vision without action is nothing. Dreams achieve meaning only when followed by deliberate effort to make them real.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_063	Swahili · East Africa	Penye nia pana ____ — Where there is will there is a ____	way	["way", "God", "water", "food"]	0	Penye nia pana njia	beginner	Determination creates possibility. The person who genuinely wants to achieve something will always find or create a path forward.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_064	Swahili · East Africa	Ukweli ni taa ya ____ — Truth is the lamp of the ____	world	["world", "night", "heart", "wise"]	0	Ukweli ni taa ya dunia	intermediate	Truth illuminates — it exposes what is hidden and guides what is lost. Without it, individuals and societies stumble in darkness.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_swa_065	Swahili · East Africa	Usiku wa manane ndipo ujanjez unapoanza — It is at ____ that cleverness begins	midnight	["midnight", "dawn", "dusk", "noon"]	0	Usiku wa manane ndipo ujanja unapoanza	veteran	The deepest wisdom and the most critical thinking emerge when the noise of the day has settled. Stillness and darkness are when true cleverness activates.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_052	Zulu · South Africa	Injobo enhle thi hlangana — A good mat is woven ____	together	["together", "slowly", "tightly", "daily"]	0	Injobo enhle thi hlangana	beginner	The best outcomes result from collaboration. A mat woven by many hands is stronger and more beautiful than one woven alone.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_053	Zulu · South Africa	Inyoni yaziwa ngezwi layo — A bird is known by its ____	call	["call", "feathers", "nest", "size"]	0	Inyoni yaziwa ngezwi layo	intermediate	You identify what something truly is by what it produces or expresses — not by how it looks. A person is known by their words and deeds.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_054	Zulu · South Africa	Izandla ziyagezana — ____ wash each other	Hands	["Hands", "Rivers", "Rains", "People"]	0	Izandla ziyagezana	beginner	Mutual assistance keeps both parties clean and functional. Reciprocity is not transactional — it is the natural order of things.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_055	Zulu · South Africa	Umuntu akalahlwa — A person is never ____	abandoned	["abandoned", "forgotten", "punished", "replaced"]	0	Umuntu akalahlwa	intermediate	No person is disposable. The Ubuntu ethic demands that every individual retains their fundamental worth regardless of what they have done or become.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_056	Zulu · South Africa	Ukuhleka akusikho ukuthanda — Laughing with someone is not the same as ____ them	loving	["loving", "trusting", "knowing", "helping"]	0	Ukuhleka akusikho ukuthanda	advanced	Shared laughter is pleasant but shallow. Do not mistake surface-level congeniality for deep love or genuine loyalty — they are fundamentally different things.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_057	Zulu · South Africa	Ingwe idla ngamabala — The leopard eats by its ____	spots	["spots", "speed", "claws", "strength"]	0	Ingwe idla ngamabala	intermediate	A person succeeds through their distinctive qualities. Your unique characteristics are not flaws to hide but assets to deploy.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_058	Zulu · South Africa	Isando esisindayo kaliwa — A heavy ____ is not thrown away	hammer	["hammer", "stone", "pot", "spear"]	0	Isando esisindayo kaliwa	advanced	Difficulty is not a reason to discard something valuable. The fact that something requires great effort is itself evidence of its worth.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_059	Zulu · South Africa	Akekho umuntu ongenasici — There is no person without a ____	flaw	["flaw", "name", "family", "shadow"]	0	Akekho umuntu ongenasici	beginner	Perfection is not a human condition. Acknowledging this prevents both self-hatred and the harsh judgment of others for their imperfections.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_zul_060	Zulu · South Africa	Ukukhuluma kuyakhiwa — Speech ____	builds	["builds", "destroys", "lies", "flows"]	0	Ukukhuluma kuyakhiwa	intermediate	Words are constructive forces. Chosen carefully, language builds trust, community and understanding. This is why speech must be treated with great care.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_051	Amharic · Ethiopia	Lijoch yemiyawodum lij new — The child who will be great can be seen when they are ____	young	["young", "alone", "hungry", "asleep"]	0	Lijoch yemiyawodum lij new	beginner	Greatness shows itself early. Natural gifts and character traits that will define a person appear in childhood — pay attention to children.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_052	Amharic · Ethiopia	Ye-imaret lijoch aysazazum — Children of the same neighbourhood do not ____	quarrel	["quarrel", "play", "share", "grow"]	0	Ye-imaret lijoch aysazazum	intermediate	People from the same community have too much shared history and interdependence to afford serious conflict. Proximity creates obligation of peace.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_053	Amharic · Ethiopia	Timirt yelem timirt — There is no education without ____	hardship	["hardship", "teachers", "books", "time"]	0	Timirt yelem timirt	advanced	Real learning requires struggle. Knowledge acquired without difficulty is rarely retained or truly understood. Challenge is the teacher.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_054	Amharic · Ethiopia	Be-ij kezore be-ij — Having given with one hand receive with the ____	other	["other", "same", "right", "heart"]	0	Be-ij kezore be-ij	beginner	Generosity creates a cycle — what you give with one hand returns through the other. Giving is not loss but investment in relationship.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_055	Amharic · Ethiopia	Sew sew nat — A person is ____	human	["human", "spirit", "earth", "water"]	0	Sew sew nat	beginner	Humanity is the defining quality. Whatever else a person may or may not have they are first and fundamentally human — deserving of dignity on that basis alone.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_056	Amharic · Ethiopia	Yewedeq lijun yalwedeq ____ yamregal — Those who love teach those who do not ____	love	["love", "know", "care", "lead"]	0	Yewedeq lijun yalwedeq amregal	intermediate	Love is not innate in all its expressions — it must be modelled and taught. Parents and communities transmit the capacity to love through example.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_057	Amharic · Ethiopia	Timirt betam tinish neger nat — Knowledge is a very ____ thing	small	["small", "heavy", "rare", "sharp"]	0	Timirt betam tinish neger nat	veteran	Knowledge appears small and lightweight — it takes up no space — yet it is the most powerful thing a person can carry. Its value is inversely proportional to its physical presence.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_eth_058	Amharic · Ethiopia	Lij ahun yetemare ____ yihonal — The child who learns now will be ____ later	wise	["wise", "strong", "rich", "old"]	0	Lij ahun yetemare huletu huleta yihonal	beginner	Investment in learning today compounds into capability tomorrow. Education is the surest path from present limitation to future possibility.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_051	Wolof · Senegal	Ku xam xam dafa xam ku xam — He who knows, knows he who ____	knows	["knows", "lies", "waits", "leads"]	0	Ku xam xam dafa xam ku xam	advanced	True knowledge is self-aware. The genuinely wise person can recognise wisdom in others — and equally recognise its absence. Wisdom sees itself.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_052	Wolof · Senegal	Lu baax dafa mel ni lu bees — What is good looks like something ____	new	["new", "old", "true", "hard"]	0	Lu baax dafa mel ni lu bees	intermediate	Genuine goodness has a freshness to it — it does not grow stale or familiar. True virtue always retains a quality of novelty and wonder.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_053	Wolof · Senegal	Boroom kër gi mooy ____  — The master of the house is the ____	foundation	["foundation", "door", "roof", "wall"]	0	Boroom kër gi mooy yëkënam	intermediate	The head of a household is the structural foundation — when that foundation is stable the whole house stands. Leadership at home determines everything.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_054	Wolof · Senegal	Nit nitay garabam — A person's cure is another ____	person	["person", "prayer", "herb", "elder"]	0	Nit nitay garabam	beginner	The most powerful healing force available to any human being is another human being. Connection, care and companionship heal what medicine cannot.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_055	Wolof · Senegal	Ku am kersa du tàmbalee ci kaw —  He who has dignity does not start from the ____	top	["top", "bottom", "middle", "side"]	0	Ku am kersa du tàmbalee ci kaw	advanced	A person of true dignity does not need to begin at the top or claim superiority — they are comfortable starting humbly because their worth is not dependent on position.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_056	Wolof · Senegal	Xam-xam dafa am ____ — Knowledge has ____	power	["power", "weight", "colour", "price"]	0	Xam-xam dafa am mbëgël	intermediate	Knowledge is not neutral — it carries real force in the world. What you know shapes what you can do and who you can become.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_wol_057	Wolof · Senegal	Jëf bu bëgg, bëgg na ci ____ — An act of love loves its ____	response	["response", "witness", "memory", "silence"]	0	Jëf bu bëgg, bëgg na ci dëkk bi	veteran	A loving act contains within itself the longing for reciprocity and belonging. Love is not just given — it inherently seeks a home in the world where it can be returned.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_051	Pan-African	If you want to go fast go alone. If you want to go far go ____	together	["together", "slowly", "early", "prepared"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	beginner	Individual effort produces speed but collective effort produces endurance and distance. The greatest achievements in human history have been collaborative.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_054	Pan-African	Rain does not fall on one ____ alone	roof	["roof", "man", "tree", "village"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	beginner	Collective experience — both hardship and blessing — is shared by entire communities. No person suffers or celebrates in complete isolation from those around them.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_055	Pan-African	He who tells the stories rules the ____	world	["world", "village", "future", "children"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	intermediate	Narrative power is real power. Whoever controls how a community understands its history, identity and possibilities controls the direction of that community.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_056	Pan-African	The axe forgets but the ____ remembers	tree	["tree", "forest", "ground", "wood"]	0	Shona proverb, Zimbabwe	intermediate	Those who cause harm often move on and forget. Those who receive harm carry the memory far longer. This asymmetry calls for empathy and accountability.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_057	Pan-African	Wisdom is like a ____ tree — no one individual can embrace it	baobab	["baobab", "palm", "mango", "acacia"]	0	Akan tradition, Ghana	intermediate	The baobab's vast trunk cannot be encircled by one person's arms. Similarly, true wisdom is too vast and communal for any single mind to fully contain.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_058	Pan-African	Knowledge is like a garden — if it is not ____ it cannot be harvested	cultivated	["cultivated", "shared", "watered", "guarded"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	intermediate	Wisdom does not grow passively. It must be actively tended through practice, teaching and application — otherwise it withers like an untended garden.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_060	Pan-African	A tree is straightened while it is ____	young	["young", "wet", "green", "small"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	beginner	Character is formed in youth. The values, habits and worldview instilled in childhood will determine the shape of the adult. Early formation is everything.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_061	Pan-African	He who runs from fire falls into ____	water	["water", "darkness", "another fire", "the river"]	0	Yoruba tradition, Nigeria	intermediate	Fleeing one problem carelessly leads to another. Panicked escape without direction and plan exchanges one danger for another equally serious one.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_062	Pan-African	Cross the river in a crowd and the crocodile won't eat ____	you	["you", "anyone", "the weak", "the slow"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	beginner	Numbers and collective movement provide safety that individual action cannot. There is genuine protective power in being part of a group.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_063	Pan-African	The forest would be silent if no bird sang except the one that sang ____	best	["best", "first", "last", "loudest"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	intermediate	Waiting for perfection before contributing your voice leaves the world impoverished. Every voice has its place in the whole — including yours.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_064	Pan-African	Do not look where you fell but where you ____	slipped	["slipped", "stood", "ran", "started"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	intermediate	The point of failure is rarely where the problem began. Trace any difficulty back to its root cause rather than focusing narrowly on the moment things went wrong.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_065	Pan-African	The strength of the crocodile is the ____	water	["water", "river", "darkness", "mud"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	advanced	Every creature's power is inseparable from its natural environment. Remove a person — or any being — from what sustains them and their strength collapses. Know what gives you power.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_066	Pan-African	A healthy ear can stand hearing sick ____	words	["words", "news", "people", "cries"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	advanced	Emotional and psychological maturity means being able to receive difficult, painful or challenging information without being destroyed by it. Build resilience through inner health.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_067	Pan-African	Speak softly and carry a big ____	stick	["stick", "heart", "knife", "drum"]	0	African oral tradition	beginner	True authority needs neither volume nor performance. The most powerful people communicate with quiet confidence, not noise — they let their capacity speak.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_068	Pan-African	By the time the fool has learned the game the players have ____	dispersed	["dispersed", "won", "cheated", "changed"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Learning too slowly in a fast-moving world means arriving after the opportunity has already passed. Adaptability and rapid learning are survival skills not luxuries.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_069	Pan-African	Wealth if you use it comes to an end; learning if you use it ____	increases	["increases", "deepens", "spreads", "stays"]	0	Swahili proverb	intermediate	Material wealth diminishes with use but knowledge compounds with application. Invest in what grows rather than what depletes.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_070	Pan-African	One who causes others to prosper will ____	prosper	["prosper", "lead", "rule", "rest"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	beginner	Those who invest in the growth of others find that prosperity returns to them. Generosity is not sacrifice — it is the most reliable investment available.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_071	Pan-African	Even the mightiest ____ must return to the sea	river	["river", "storm", "eagle", "king"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	intermediate	All power and greatness ultimately return to their source. No individual or force remains elevated forever — humility before this truth is wisdom.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_072	Pan-African	It takes a village to raise a ____	child	["child", "harvest", "home", "elder"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	beginner	No parent raises a child alone — the whole community participates in the formation of every young person. This is both responsibility and privilege.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_073	Pan-African	Not all who wander in the bush are ____	lost	["lost", "hunting", "afraid", "alone"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	advanced	Movement without an apparent destination is not always aimlessness. Sometimes the most purposeful journeys do not follow straight paths or visible roads.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_074	Pan-African	A short man is not a ____	boy	["boy", "fool", "child", "servant"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	intermediate	Physical stature — or any external limitation — does not determine the substance of a person. Respect is owed on the basis of character not appearance.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_075	Pan-African	The same sun that melts wax hardens ____	clay	["clay", "stone", "soil", "iron"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Identical circumstances produce opposite results depending on the nature of what they act upon. Your response to adversity — not the adversity itself — determines your outcome.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_076	Pan-African	War has no ____ — only survivors and losses	winners	["winners", "rules", "end", "reason"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	advanced	Conflict destroys all parties involved — those who appear to win still lose something irreplaceable. The truly wise avoid war rather than seek victory in it.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_077	Pan-African	A bird that flies off the earth and lands on an anthill is still on the ____	ground	["ground", "earth", "farm", "road"]	0	Igbo tradition, Nigeria	veteran	Incremental progress that merely trades one low position for another slightly less low position is not true elevation. Real progress requires genuine transformation of circumstance.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_078	Pan-African	The eye never forgets what the ____ has seen	heart	["heart", "mind", "mouth", "ear"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	advanced	What has been witnessed and felt at the deepest level cannot be erased. The most powerful memories are not stored in the mind but registered in the emotional core of a person.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_pan_080	Pan-African	The one who tells the stories determines the ____	future	["future", "truth", "law", "names"]	0	Pan-African oral tradition	veteran	Narrative shapes reality. Those who control the stories a community tells about itself — its heroes, its enemies, its purpose — effectively control what that community becomes.	2026-05-24 00:17:27.803645+00
yd_ibo_004	Igbo · Nigeria	A man who does not know where the rain began to beat him cannot know where it ____	stopped	["stopped", "started", "fell", "ended"]	0	Onye na-amaghị ebe ozizi malitere iku ya n'isi, o nweghị ike ịmara ebe ọ kwụsịrị	intermediate	Without understanding the origin of a problem you cannot identify where it ends. Tracing difficulty back to its source is the only reliable way to address it completely.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_005	Igbo · Nigeria	When the elders are in the house the goat does not give birth by the ____	roadside	["roadside", "river", "market", "forest"]	0	Ọ bụrụ na ndị okenye nọ n'ulo, ewu anaghị amị n'ụzọ	intermediate	The presence of experienced elders prevents reckless or inappropriate behaviour. Communities function better when wisdom and experience are actively present rather than absent or ignored.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_006	Igbo · Nigeria	The lizard that jumped from the high iroko tree said it would praise itself if no one else ____	did	["did", "watched", "cared", "followed"]	0	Ogwumagala si na o were onwe ya isi, ọ bụrụ na onye ọzọ emeghị ya	advanced	When no one else will recognise your achievement you must be willing to acknowledge it yourself. Self-acknowledgment in the absence of external validation is not arrogance — it is necessary dignity.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_007	Igbo · Nigeria	When the righteous man sins he is judged more harshly than the ____	wicked	["wicked", "stranger", "poor", "young"]	0	Mgbe onye ọma mee ihe ọjọọ, a na-akụ ya ikpe karịa onye ọjọọ	advanced	Those who set high standards for themselves are judged more harshly when they fall short. The expectation of virtue creates a stricter standard of accountability than the expectation of nothing.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_008	Igbo · Nigeria	A toad does not run in the daytime unless something is chasing ____	it	["it", "him", "her", "them"]	0	Ọchịchọ anaghị agba ọsọ n'ehihie ma ọ bụrụ na ihe na-achụ ya	beginner	Unusual behaviour in the light of day signals that something is wrong beneath the surface. When things act out of character there is always a reason worth investigating.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_009	Igbo · Nigeria	The man who carries another on his back does not know how far he has ____	walked	["walked", "carried", "travelled", "suffered"]	0	Onye na-ebu ibe ya n'azụ amaghị ebe ọ gara n'ụzọ	intermediate	Those who provide support to others often cannot accurately assess the full cost of what they are giving. Proximity to effort distorts our perception of its weight and difficulty.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_010	Igbo · Nigeria	When a new dance comes to town the old men are the last to ____	learn	["learn", "watch", "judge", "leave"]	0	Mgbe egwu ọhụrụ bịa n'obodo, ndị okenye bụ nke ikpeazụ ịmụta ya	beginner	Established traditions and authorities are slow to embrace new ways. Those most invested in existing systems are typically the last to recognise the value of what replaces them.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
yd_ibo_011	Igbo · Nigeria	The young cannot teach the elders how the ____ tastes	morning	["morning", "palm wine", "night", "harvest"]	0	Ndị ọcha anaghị akụzị ndị okenye otuto nke ọnụọgụgụ	advanced	The young lack the accumulated experience needed to judge things that only time and living can teach. Some knowledge simply cannot be transferred — it must be lived into.	2026-04-19 00:36:49.621376+00
